🗺️ PONG ROADMAP (Godot + GDScript)
✅ STEP 1: Set Up Your Godot Project
Create a new 2D project in Godot.

Make a new scene called Main.tscn.

Set up a Node2D as the root.

✅ Skills you learn:

Godot project structure

Scene creation

Node types

✅ STEP 2: Add the Ball
Add a CharacterBody2D or Area2D node (for the ball).

Add a Sprite2D and CollisionShape2D as children.

Give it a circle sprite and a collision shape.

✅ Skills you learn:

Using nodes and children

Setting up sprites and collisions

✅ STEP 3: Make the Ball Move
Attach a script to the ball.

Use a Vector2 for direction.

Move the ball using _physics_process(delta).

gdscript
Copy
Edit
var velocity = Vector2(200, 150)

func _physics_process(delta):
    position += velocity * delta
✅ Skills you learn:

Movement logic

Delta time

Vectors

✅ STEP 4: Add Walls
Add StaticBody2D or CollisionPolygon2D nodes to make top and bottom walls.

Add collision shapes so the ball bounces off.

✅ Skills you learn:

Static bodies

Collision handling

✅ STEP 5: Bounce the Ball
Detect collision and reverse ball direction on Y axis when it hits top/bottom.

gdscript
Copy
Edit
if position.y <= 0 or position.y >= screen_height:
    velocity.y *= -1
✅ Skills you learn:

If statements

Simple physics response

✅ STEP 6: Add Player Paddles
Create two CharacterBody2D nodes for paddles.

Add Sprite2D and CollisionShape2D to each.

Position them on the left and right.

✅ Skills you learn:

More node setup

Positioning elements manually

✅ STEP 7: Move Paddles with Input
Attach a script to each paddle.

Use Input.is_action_pressed("ui_up") / "ui_down".

gdscript
Copy
Edit
func _physics_process(delta):
    var direction = 0
    if Input.is_action_pressed("ui_up"):
        direction -= 1
    if Input.is_action_pressed("ui_down"):
        direction += 1

    position.y += direction * speed * delta
✅ Skills you learn:

Input handling

Player movement

✅ STEP 8: Make Ball Bounce Off Paddles
Use CollisionShape2D or body_entered signal.

When ball hits a paddle, reverse X direction:

gdscript
Copy
Edit
velocity.x *= -1
✅ Skills you learn:

Collision detection

Signal use (optional)

✅ STEP 9: Score System
Add Label nodes to show score for each player.

When the ball goes off-screen (left or right), update the score and reset the ball.

gdscript
Copy
Edit
if position.x < 0:
    player2_score += 1
    reset_ball()

if position.x > screen_width:
    player1_score += 1
    reset_ball()
✅ Skills you learn:

Score tracking

Ball reset logic

